The bare and both G9 runs now have genuine script-owned transcripts, but each contains only four HTTP 403 error records and therefore zero valid oracle attempts. This does not count as hardness evidence. I’m recording it as an external validation blocker while keeping the locally verified generator intact; there is no mathematical basis for rejecting the family.
